From 017fc024026906566991a94339288038b590a903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:56:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] split worker-thread gates out of
 agent/tool_executor.py (FILE_LINES headroom)

tool_executor.py sat at exactly 2000 lines, the code-health FILE_LINES cap, so any
addition failed the ratchet. Move the authorization gate, the start-order gate and
worker-tid registration / interrupt fan-out verbatim into agent/tool_worker_gates.py
and re-export them from agent.tool_executor, which stays the import path for callers
and tests. The moved code keeps the agent.tool_executor logger, so record names and
levels are unchanged. tool_executor.py is now 1808 lines.

No fork-only block of that size exists (the fork adds ~40 net lines to this file), so
the moved block is upstream code that is byte-identical to upstream and has not
changed there since early October.

Card: t_01a1c895eb8f4f8f
